  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the biennium, ILO support will continue to reiterate the significance of (decent) employment as a driving factor (not mere result) behind economic growth that needs to be more strongly promoted within SADC member states.  International labour standards underlie decent work, and include those concerning freedom of association, collective bargaining, and non-discrimination, enhance governance and democratic processes and add impetus towards inclusive and sustainable socio-economic progress.  In addition, ILO support will highlight that international labour standards enhance respect for the rule of law while promoting a culture of transparency, joint decision-making, and mutual respect.</narrative>
  </description>
